ATTACK 5 -- PDF SECTION 4.2 COMPLIANCE AUDIT OF THE SURVIVOR (M6)
==============================================================================
  DAG = (7, 0, 1, 8, 3, 8, 7, 5, -1, 8, 9, 9)
bayes_net bounds: OK (12 features, 11 feature edges)
  rule 6..12 features          : n = 12  -> OK
  rule 2..5 states per feature : (5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 4, 5, 4, 4)  bad=[] -> OK
  rule >=2 feature edges       : 11 edges -> OK
  rule <=2 parents incl. Y     : max = 2 -> OK
  rule Y is root of every node : Y is a parent of all 12 feature nodes and has no parents -> OK
  rule acyclic                 : Kahn visiting 12/12 nodes -> OK
    explicit acyclic witness (one valid topological order): ['euler', 'vruns', 'vdom', 'aspect', 'mr', 'br', 'bl', 'tl', 'tc', 'tr', 'ml', 'mc']
    structural proof: the 12 nodes have <=1 feature parent each, so the
    feature graph has <=12 arcs over 12 nodes; root = euler only.  Every
    path is monotonically directed away from euler / the band roots, so no
    arc closes back on a node already on the path -> acyclic by construction.
  rule no hidden variables     : all 12 nodes are observed features -> OK
  rule no auto structure learn : the DAG is one of 9 hand-authored structures -> OK

  RISK FLAGS:
    * feature-edge count = 11; with <=1 feature parent per
      node the hard maximum is 12, so only 1 more edge could be added.
      Any extra conditioning requires REMOVING an edge (M6 itself removed mc->mr).
    * euler_topology is a feature parent of ml and mr; the node euler has no
      feature parent, so every added edge must respect that euler stays a root.

